s no weight under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13. Because no advisory identifier was named, this is a gap in the bundle and not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation, and the missing artifact does not cap confidence. Your fallback that the rider agreed to the ECP routing also fails: EV-CHAT-00501 holds zero messages, so there is no recorded rider instruction, no waypoint_hint and no named road, and POL-RD-04's corroboration test is undecidable on the record — the clause is unavailable and the defence is discarded under POL-RD-08.\n\nThe two ERP lines are genuine crossings (the trace's nearest fix lies 0 m from each gantry, inside the 250 m radius) and the airport surcharge of 0.00 is not a defect, so there is no billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4) and no referral on that ground. No profile field has been used to establish anything about this trip (POL-GEN-01). Confidence is 0.90: the deciding facts — the measured excess and the fare arithmetic — are carried by the GPS trace, the trip record and the fare breakdown, each at weight 1.0, so the cap is 1.0, above the 0.70 floor.\n\nOutcome: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 14.50 to the rider; the driver receives no compensation (the billed distance equals the traced distance, so POL-RD-04's compensation limb has no shortfall to work on)."
