    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver — the amount contested on this trip was SGD 39.00, and SGD 14.50 of it is returned to the rider; the remainder of the charge stands.\n\nFARE ARITHMETIC. The trip was booked on an upfront quote (EV-FARE-00501, fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 24.50), so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run: the distance and time lines were fixed at booking and a detour cannot be turned into a recomputed distance fare. The rider's remedy is the amount by which the SGD 39.00 actually charged exceeds the SGD 24.50 quote plus the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09. Those properly chargeable lines are nil: the two ECP gantries (SGD 3.00 each, SGD 6.00 together) sit off the booked optimal corridor (on_optimal_route false for both; the optimal route — PIE to Kallang then Nicoll Highway — carried no ERP), and the airport surcharge is SGD 0.00. So SGD 39.00 − SGD 24.50 − SGD 0.00 = SGD 14.50, which is the refund and requires no further rounding. The SGD 6.00 of ECP ERP is already comprehended inside that 14.50 and is not added on top of it (POL-RD-09(1)); both advocates agree on this and I accept it.\n\nDEVIATION FINDING. A deviation is established on this trip's own trace: EV-GPS-00501 measures 25.4 km (trace_distance_km governs; the trip record's 25.4 km is a rounded copy) against a booked optimal of 19.6 km — an excess of 5.8 km, 29.59% — which clears the POL-RD-01 gates of 20% and 0.8 km. It is below the 50% and 8.0 km materiality tests, so POL-RD-06's material-deviation consequences do not engage, and in any event the driver's profile is clean (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 250: no repeat pattern, no conduct referral). On an upfront-quoted trip this finding does not move the money, because the distance and time lines were already fixed.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATIONS. The account that the PIE was 'crawling' is backed by no artifact: the traffic advisory for this trip, EV-ADVIS-00501-01, is MISSING — weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. Under POL-RD-13, POL-RD-03 cannot be run, the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and because the driver names no advisory identifier the missing advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than the POL-RD-10(5) contradiction that would force escalation; the excess therefore stands at the measured figure. The account that the rider agreed to the ECP route is equally unsupported: the chat log EV-CHAT-00501 holds zero messages, so there is no recorded rider instruction and no waypoint_hint, POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run and that clause is unavailable. I note that nothing corroborates the rider's own account of the conversation either; the outcome rests on the ledger arithmetic, not on either party's recollection.\n\nESCALATION, REFERRALS AND CONFIDENCE. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes (163 fixes, 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0), so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged and no other POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The ruling rests entirely on artifacts of full weight (EV-FARE-00501, EV-GPS-00501, EV-TRIP-00501), so the confidence cap is 1.0; the missing advisory carries no fact and does not cap it. My confidence is 0.90. No referral is warranted: the two gantry lines are genuine crossings matched to within 250 m (fix indices 101 and 130), so there is no billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4), and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c). No driver compensation is payable: the billed distance (25.4 km) matches the trace, so POL-RD-04's unbilled-distance limb does not arise, and on an upfront-quoted trip the driver's unrecovered detour cost is not recoverable from the rider under POL-RD-11."
